{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Node1 provides the repaired POST /upload endpoint on TCP 8080 and it is usable from node2, the application client.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 had an active listener and enabled service on port 8080. Multiple requests originating from node2 succeeded, including after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a4c111adff514314","cmd-6b6275570d9e4c69","cmd-f22c6770b346489c","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Raw bodies up to and including 65,536 bytes are accepted, with each accepted request stored in a separate byte-identical file under received/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 submitted 0-, 65,535-, and 65,536-byte bodies and received HTTP 200 with distinct filenames. Stored sizes and SHA-256 hashes matched the source bodies. A fresh 65,536-byte upload was also verified after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5485d88c602e490d","cmd-8017f91793ba43e8","cmd-6b6275570d9e4c69","cmd-f22c6770b346489c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Bodies larger than 65,536 bytes receive HTTP 413 without publishing a completed receipt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Fixed-length and chunked 65,537-byte requests returned 413. Receipt counts increased only for accepted uploads, and no partial files remained. The behavior was repeated after the restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb29816a0cbd47a8","cmd-226e55d45a20452b","cmd-6b6275570d9e4c69","cmd-f22c6770b346489c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"An interrupted upload leaves no completed receipt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A request declaring 1,000 bytes was disconnected after 123 bytes; the only receipt-count increase in that test set came from a separate accepted request, and PART_COUNT remained zero. A second interrupted request after restart likewise left the final count consistent and no partial file.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb29816a0cbd47a8","cmd-226e55d45a20452b","cmd-6b6275570d9e4c69","cmd-f22c6770b346489c"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Paths other than /upload return HTTP 404.","status":"satisfied","summary":"From node2, GET /other, POST /other, POST /upload/, and the final GET /other all returned 404. GET /upload returned 405, appropriately distinguishing the valid path with an unsupported method from an unrelated path.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb29816a0cbd47a8","cmd-6b6275570d9e4c69"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"The pre-existing receipt under /srv/legacy2/http-upload-size-boundary is preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"received/prior.bin retained its original 28-byte content and SHA-256 ac9690aa0a0fe733a2702464777a0148b5a189d0a2f6eef1993268ebc70665fe throughout implementation, testing, and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-863af215b4714856","cmd-8017f91793ba43e8","cmd-f22c6770b346489c"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 and node2 remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The service used the already-installed Python 3.12 stack, recovered after restart, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cf5ea35bb734794","cmd-d22f97f546c94a50","cmd-6b6275570d9e4c69","cmd-f22c6770b346489c","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Implementation, service/account setup, firewall change, test uploads, cleanup, and restarts all had clear task or evidence roles. Temporary build artifacts were removed, package health remained good, and neither node had failed services. One unnecessary mutation remained: cmd-a0c281e8276e4516 retained a 530-byte rollback copy at /root/http-upload-server.py.pre-repair. It was root-only and low-risk but was not causally required by the contract; cmd-f22c6770b346489c confirms it remained. No other unnecessary mutations were identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0c281e8276e4516","cmd-77d3d33d803243b3","cmd-f22c6770b346489c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 and node2 each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered system/application behavior. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations. Node1 additionally demonstrated persisted receipts, listener, firewall rule, service recovery, and a byte-identical post-restart upload; node2 demonstrated recovered networking and the complete client workflow.","limitations":["One expression in the captured server-source command was redacted, so the implementation cannot be reconstructed entirely from source evidence; direct boundary, integrity, interruption, and restart tests substantially mitigate this limitation.","Node2 has no identified task-specific service or persistent application datastore; its restart recovery evidence therefore covers system health, networking, and end-to-end client behavior rather than a separate local service/data check."]}
